find - walk a tree looking for names

SYNOPSIS
    find [DIRECTORY] [-name PATTERN]

DESCRIPTION
    Descends from the directory given, or the current one, printing every
    path it meets.

      -name PATTERN   only names matching the pattern, with * and ?
      -type f | d     only files, or only directories

    Symbolic links are not followed, which is what stops a loop from being
    infinite.

SEE ALSO
    grep, ls
